  "_comment": "Two LoRAs at once — a style and a subject. Chained rather than merged: the second loader takes the first's model and clip, so their strengths stay independent and either can be dialled back without touching the other. Stacking is where LoRAs usually go wrong; two at full strength fight, and the second one wins in a way that looks like the first was never loaded.",
